# Readme used by the start.desktop app
[type=file perms=644] etc/desktop_files/README.txt={
Welcome to QNX 8.0 Non-Commercial!

This QNX 8 target is now ready for your QNX applications. There are
some sample applications included here to help you get started with
development. Find the source code for most of them at gitlab.com/qnx.

Here's how to run some of the bundled samples:

|-------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| $ gles2-gears                 | Displays hardware-rendered content using OpenGL ES 2.x.  |
| $ gles2-maze                  | Shows how to use texture, vertex, and fragment shaders.  |
| $ camera_example3_viewfinder  | Displays a simulated camera signal or live camera feed.  |
| $ st                          | The default terminal. Run it to open a new instance.     |
|-------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|

(You can use ALT-TAB to switch between windows.)

To get Started
 - Try the developer desktop to compile apps directly on QNX
 - Target and Host system users connect over SSH or serial terminal and setup
   Momentics or VS Code IDE

Documentation
 - Visit qnx.com/developer/docs/qnxeverywhere/ for technical documentation
 - Visit github.com/qnx for sample app source code
 - Visit oss.qnx.com for list of open-source ports

Community Feedback
 - Find the community in Discord at https://discord.gg/Jj4EkkrFTT, 
   on Reddit at https://reddit.com/r/QNX, or log an issue 
   at https://gitlab.com/qnx.
}

[type=file perms=755] etc/desktop_files/display_readme.sh={
#!/bin/bash

clear
cat /system/etc/desktop_files/README.txt | more
echo "Press any key to exit..."
read -n 1 -s
exit
}
